    {
      "title": "Have or has plus the past participle",
      "description": "Form affirmative and negative present perfect sentences.",
      "objective": "Form affirmative and negative present perfect sentences.",
      "content": "The present perfect uses have or has plus a past participle. Use have with I, you, we, and they; use has with he, she, and it.",
      "examples": [
        "I have finished my homework.",
        "She has seen that film."
      ],
      "commonErrors": [
        "He have finished. -> He has finished.",
        "They have went home. -> They have gone home."
      ],
      "guidedPractice": "Choose have or has for the subject, then select the correct past participle.",
      "summary": "Present perfect form is subject + have/has + past participle.",
      "questions": [
        {
          "type": "MULTIPLE_CHOICE",
          "questionText": "I ___ finished my homework.",
