      "description": "Use present perfect time words for recent actions and unfinished periods.",
      "objective": "Use present perfect time words for recent actions and unfinished periods.",
      "content": "Use just for a recent action, already for an earlier-than-expected action, and yet in questions and negatives. Use the present perfect with today, this week, and other unfinished periods.",
      "examples": [
        "She has just arrived.",
        "Have you finished yet?",
        "I have already eaten."
      ],
      "commonErrors": [
        "I just have finished. -> I have just finished.",
        "Did you finish yet? -> Have you finished yet?"
