    {
      "title": "Present perfect and past simple time contrasts",
      "description": "Choose between present perfect and past simple with clear time references.",
      "objective": "Choose between present perfect and past simple with clear time references.",
      "content": "Use present perfect for an unfinished period or a present result without a finished time. Use past simple with finished times such as yesterday, last year, or in 2020.",
      "examples": [
        "I have visited Hue this year.",
        "I visited Hue last year."
      ],
      "commonErrors": [
        "I have seen him yesterday. -> I saw him yesterday.",
        "She went to Paris this year. -> She has been to Paris this year when the year is unfinished."
      ],
      "guidedPractice": "Circle the time expression. Finished past time selects past simple; unfinished time or a present result selects present perfect.",
